Subject: Compose wider and deeper inline caches with a megamorphic fallback

What this does
  Extends the foundational property inline caches with an explicitly configurable
  per-site width, including a four-entry configuration, and caches plain data
  properties found on a receiver grandparent prototype. Sites that exhaust their
  bounded entries can use a direct-mapped runtime fallback keyed by receiver shape
  and property name. The shipping width remains one entry per site.

Why we need it
  Polymorphic React Native workloads repeatedly encounter a small set of object
  shapes, while megamorphic workloads otherwise repeat the same prototype walk.
  Wider entries and validated depth-two guards preserve the cheap monomorphic path
  while giving explicitly enabled builds a way to reduce those repeated walks.

What it adds
  Four-entry polymorphic sites       - compile-time width without adaptive expansion.
  Depth-two prototype reads           - guarded by receiver and intermediate shapes.
  Megamorphic fallback cache          - weak, direct-mapped, and shape-free safe.
  IC statistics                       - available only with QJS_ICSTAT.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No. This extends the existing inline-cache opcodes and metadata format from the
  foundational cache patch.

